i hope you still have the file with your uid and the new name in the
save directory. if you played nethack before 3.0 you may have noticed
that when became a new person and changed your name and saved the game,
that you when restored the game you were yourself (old name) again.
nethack 3.0 changed all that and a consequence of that is the fact that
when you undergo a name change the change is real!  "daver" seems to be
your default name, however you can access your "newname" game in several
ways and i'll mention 2 here:

1) if the enviroment variable NETHACKOPTIONS is available to you then
    simply change your name there (remember to change to it back after
    the game is finished). this would look something like (unix csh):
setenv NETHACKOPTIONS "name:newname"       ... with other stuff possible.

2) the simplest solution is to access the game telling nethack that you
    are using an assumed name via the "-u" switch as in:
nethack -u newname
    where "newname" is, of course, your new name.
